#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198154 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2aee319-68d6-54f7-8023-b24d32610bc4" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products of Special Sets in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "eae94514-cd92-5405-90b1-ee09dad18e13" :question/math-academy-id "e-13162" :question/problem "Sketch a representation of the set $S = \\mathbb{Z} \\times \\mathbb{N}$ in the Cartesian plane." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A \\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B = \\big\\{(a,b) \\::\\: a\\in A,\\, b\\in B\\big\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS = \\mathbb{Z} \\times \\mathbb{N}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ whose $x$-coordinate is an integer number and whose $y$-coordinate is a natural number.\n\n$$\nS=\n\\Big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: x\\in \\mathbb Z,\\, y\\in \\mathbb N\\Big\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider $S_1\\subset S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any integer number and whose $y$-coordinate equals ${\\color{red}{1}}.$\n\n$$\nS_1 = \\Big\\{ (x, {\\color{red}{1}}) \\: : \\: x\\in \\mathbb Z\\Big\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent $S_1$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/6b/6b63e973bbcc3e25d601a1f6cef97f5a00cc22e738c46d04a1ac06851421894e.png)\n\nNext, consider $S_2\\subset S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any integer number and whose $y$-coordinate equals ${\\color{blue}{2}}.$\n\n$$\nS_2 = \\Big\\{ (x,{\\color{blue}{2}}) \\: : \\: x\\in \\mathbb Z\\Big\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent $S_2$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/f2/f24ce8f7610d096c795a8a74b0b714b720c36442042c28b66432d6b2102fb9d4.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $S_3,S_4,S_5,\\ldots,$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup {S}_{4}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in N}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $\\mathbb{Z} \\times \\mathbb{N}$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/c9/c999c61d8ffbb27d47272811e32340cef3253b4730e684be10615487a8b27200.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198169 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3a2b291-c6dd-58c8-a10f-d851511d7bfc" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "bb40c174-3739-50df-835e-5d47c9902d5b" :question/math-academy-id "e-13192" :question/problem "Sketch a representation of the set $S = \\{1, 2\\} \\times (0, 1)$ in the Cartesian plane." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A \\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B = \\big\\{(a,b) \\::\\: a\\in A,\\, b\\in B\\big\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS = \\{1,2\\} \\times (0,1)\n$$\n\ncontains every point in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ whose $x$-coordinate is either $1$ or $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $(0,1).$\n\n$$\nS=\n\\Big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: x\\in \\{{\\color{red}{1}},{\\color{blue}{2}}\\},\\, y\\in (0,1) \\Big\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider $S_1\\subset S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals ${\\color{red}{1}}$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $(0,1).$\n\n$$\nS_1 = \\Big\\{ ({\\color{red}{1}},y) \\: : \\: y \\in(0,1) \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/56/56f200fce557749a56b9b5b51bc670da5f8c7f2cdb0196392ee80efcd6be980a.png)\n\nNext, consider $S_2\\subset S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals ${\\color{blue}{2}}$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $(0,1).$\n\n$$\nS_2 = \\big\\{ ({\\color{blue}{2}},y) \\: : \\: y \\in(0,1) \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/f9/f96074cc265bba6eb59717364d2aa5390fdccea4d398fe5ae0b99f7ad82f0b93.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS = S_1\\cup S_2\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the two line segments shown below.\n\n![](images/0c/0c0529aaa680b4b572d17f2cfbfb76d805134e72c50ab3ed469286cc025185a3.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198205 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6290e701-b4ea-5a86-ab7e-7371c5bdc11e" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "aa337681-5d8c-5ea1-b0fe-5d8cd15040a7" :question/math-academy-id "e-13320" :question/problem "Sketch a representation of the set $\\,\\displaystyle \\bigcup_{i \\in I} X_i$ in the Cartesian plane given that $I = [-1,1] \\subset \\mathbb{R}$ and $X_i = \\{ i \\} \\times [0, \\, i^2].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n\\bigcup_{i \\in I} A_i = \\big\\{ x \\: : \\: x \\in A_k \\:\\:\\textrm{for at least one}\\:\\: k \\in I \\big\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=-0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\nX_{-0.5} = \\{ -0.5 \\} \\times [0, 0.25] = \\big\\{ (-0.5,k) \\: : \\: k \\in [0, 0.25] \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(-0.5, 0)$ to the point $(-0.5,0.25)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/cc/ccc75eac899efcab1d0b6fde12609a3ea8f61d6fec74c739ef3393fad32645a9.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\nX_i = \\{ i \\} \\times [0, i^2] = \\big\\{ (i,k) \\: : \\: k \\in [0, i^2] \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i, i^2).$ \n\n![](images/60/60c98be5d97748e9285bb5e9c30bba9781a5ef99245789718a7828b18a6df8fb.png)\n\n \n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following figure that represents the union $\\displaystyle \\bigcup_{i \\in I} X_i{:}$\n\n![](images/b3/b3a61d686c78c76a4f461c1c771437d31030339b634661da8b8dc4f492db55eb.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198206 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5793f07d-e0de-5707-a5e1-32d657244e0b" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Intersections of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "67569060-2f33-5a8d-ae73-690742d3d318" :question/math-academy-id "e-13321" :question/problem "Let $I = [0,1] \\subset \\mathbb{R}$ and $X_i = [-i, 0] \\times [-1,1].$ Sketch a representation of $\\displaystyle \\bigcap_{i \\in I} X_i$ in the Cartesian plane." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n\\bigcap_{i \\in I} A_i = \\big\\{ x \\: : \\: x \\in A_k \\:\\:\\textrm{for all}\\:\\: k \\in I \\big\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\nX_{0.5} = [-0.5,0] \\times [-1, 1] = \\big\\{ (a,b) \\: : \\: a \\in [-0.5, 0], b \\in [-1, 1] \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(-0.5, -1),$ $(-0.5, 1),$ $(0, 1),$ and $(0, -1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/8a/8ad650cb3f2fa4da920a442e8cc1b24af5027595cba4e43138eff2126cf4c102.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\nX_i = [-i, 0] \\times [-1,1] = \\big\\{ (a,b) \\: : \\: a \\in [-i, 0], b \\in [-1, 1] \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(-i,-1),$ $(-i,1),$ $(0, 1),$ and $(0, -1).$\n\n![](images/a3/a37cfa508cf3a60536084fbc1e57c5aeac3414904d2ad72ef1deda85dc4eddd8.png)\n\n \n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the line segment $\\{0\\}\\times [-1,1]{:}$\n\n![](images/5e/5e9a611629f4370c57e77a057439c759670afa17c14c4b2339e1d471f616ea72.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5793f07d-e0de-5707-a5e1-32d657244e0b" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Intersections of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "420ca287-1bd5-5cf5-80e7-612cf6caac77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a2/a2786a8cfb41d8fb352c95dc36688fb2eff4773680be54be9dd3d1c696ae588a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282256} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6e8cc9-60ac-506f-b55d-cb773490aa5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e5/e5ed1251cb899e92d9f2e7dd6111140b07556432b5240fa5a9efacd33ce19989.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283313} {:answer/id #uuid "c213aae1-d722-5e7f-bb08-993b4d40f7a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∅,$ the empty set" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283376} {:answer/id #uuid "e970391b-4697-5a81-a74c-2cdcd11b0b96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3b/3b3d7d98bdc1c336c9151bff06f7d07bea7e2228efb253b0fc16cdd2de1faa99.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283727} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5fdcd2-a3ab-5862-9963-4921623b0e36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4f/4fa495b2b7e5528f5aa70abe8ce778fc0c1e7d5bcd4a9b855a72ee1469ed5f01.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c213aae1-d722-5e7f-bb08-993b4d40f7a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∅,$ the empty set" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283376} :answer-field/id #uuid "13465282-12df-5e6a-8807-c1cf998f6b1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283975}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "721c193d-86ea-5b03-af3e-92f2411e1ced" :question/math-academy-id "q-175295" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,2]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times \\{-i\\}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}=[0,1]\\times \\{-1\\}=\\{(k,-1)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(0,-1)$ to the point $(1,-1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/a3/a39443fd1b3764ff60c0c052085134ad7eeda6759c07c4d936fc03cd121f72dd.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times \\{-i\\}=\\{(k,-i)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(0,-i)$ to the point $(i,-i).$ \n\n![](images/7f/7f18af14c55acc4bc2cd63b601dba0bde3cd51c0284b398b401c854537003926.png)\n\nThere are no points that lie in all sets. Therefore, the intersection of the indexed sets is $∅,$ the empty set."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284731 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5793f07d-e0de-5707-a5e1-32d657244e0b" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Intersections of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bcf01ad-407e-5646-91fd-c53d9726302f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∅,$ the empty set" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281800} {:answer/id #uuid "1ab6ca2e-602c-5534-9b0c-f929ecbadc74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/71/71e38fd694074e4c8d778ad7428504ce4ebde9304a7e9c11183bd0b4c8c0ce90.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281932} {:answer/id #uuid "3aa4eac6-6ac8-5052-86c3-0a3080a0655d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0a/0a3bb1509f0c861b7eb5b2718f51719b3b2052ffbddb089922c6b2d84e365586.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282206} {:answer/id #uuid "4b39264b-403f-50f9-9c35-e390b37f1631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ab/ab2520b1ee68acbd46dc0984264bdbb9107e9ddd84a9666ba38770aabc31bb9b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282334} {:answer/id #uuid "50d1fe84-3a20-51f4-a093-f352af7e07c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/21/21def8c03fa64fa3e24d010489284a13786c3f237271228ac16f6226ecf57fa5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bcf01ad-407e-5646-91fd-c53d9726302f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∅,$ the empty set" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281800} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d9207f9-396e-5c3f-881c-5a60cbda763b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "94a67e20-d41d-58c4-acb4-f44eaa2400ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-175302" :question/problem "Let $I=[1,2]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,2-i]\\times \\{i\\}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}=[0,2-1]\\times \\{1\\}=[0,1]\\times \\{1\\}=\\{(k,1)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(0,1)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/dd/ddb7039dfcdbc2ef4070ce732c635a48194b6675cc3c78de6267e656c5e8387a.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,2-i]\\times \\{i\\}=\\{(k,i)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,2-i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(0,i)$ to the point $(2-i,i).$ \n\n![](images/e8/e83644a2f0de96ee58ea893028bb7a42681ee71a15d194f2b344c4c15f60fafe.png)\n\nThere are no points that lie in all sets. Therefore, the intersection of the indexed sets is $∅,$ the empty set."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284732 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5793f07d-e0de-5707-a5e1-32d657244e0b" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Intersections of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "507b83d3-3e2a-5514-a671-6db7d9a1af3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0b/0b689347086db4bf406a17c633b83dbc924d4c4963a64a2ca0efa7321bd6e1b3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282379} {:answer/id #uuid "b51d2528-d959-584a-bb39-a8873b816449" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c8/c8024f88915b3d2d4cc83a75e95df538973d574703faf2cc16ee4ea31f82c074.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283261} {:answer/id #uuid "c8768701-2611-5572-ba85-af574006e676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∅,$ the empty set" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283444} {:answer/id #uuid "d5dc9218-2c4b-5dc0-b73b-6ef3b7ad141a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f7/f74ac291edafc3808c7bb195f5295f50f5bac7a7d9db45310f66df95288e92cd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283550} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d89253-969a-59ed-a919-347b247ee794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/23/23970d1fbb8aaf33240272aa47741d675d114969fff75576f28413f8668b76b9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8768701-2611-5572-ba85-af574006e676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∅,$ the empty set" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283444} :answer-field/id #uuid "c76e8772-b796-5444-bc88-bb4d988c7d0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284287}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c5209ef-4d34-523c-9629-2fd348b5c16f" :question/math-academy-id "q-175303" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [0,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi i)].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=\\frac{1}{2},$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1/2}=\\{\\frac{1}{2}\\}\\times [0,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})]=\\{\\frac{1}{2}\\}\\times [0,1]=\\{(\\frac{1}{2},k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(\\frac{1}{2},0)$ to the point $(\\frac{1}{2},1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/28/2827c5b33e84aff775d8bcc7ca98492afb220dda3a52fec4166afaa4da187d66.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [0,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi i)]=\\{(i,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi k))\\,:\\,k\\in [0,i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi i)).$ \n\n![](images/5a/5a108a3c0cdf37a072d135674b6ffdb3894b8c5ba142604ea7a434b0f42245f5.png)\n\nThere are no points that lie in all sets. Therefore, the intersection of the indexed sets is $∅,$ the empty set."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5793f07d-e0de-5707-a5e1-32d657244e0b" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Intersections of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e0f6a9a-0e22-5668-8ad8-105b92dd4850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∅,$ the empty set" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281813} {:answer/id #uuid "4183f7dc-bde7-5907-934c-fbc7c21195dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/33c6eba539c7bc77e4c349c444da281fb3945aeb9f48018986e8c6373bc0e3b5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282253} {:answer/id #uuid "58a450f2-da57-50a4-bbbc-2a3816e2d994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/34/34a3addbdcf3d5348805f494ed2e427f21f6ad424b0d9d2a411dae9f99b2fb7a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282442} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa6ab8f-f730-505b-b347-f9d0abd74ad8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/eb/ebd57b72a8e825778bce33f84bcbec2a0bd8d852a5b2ce25a707224b39d07f99.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282741} {:answer/id #uuid "b504a825-6fbd-5629-9632-3e6714ee063e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0d/0d4597773001223e64f19e1db23c441cc7d4ffb1481c564b63f456fa05e4a0ed.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58a450f2-da57-50a4-bbbc-2a3816e2d994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/34/34a3addbdcf3d5348805f494ed2e427f21f6ad424b0d9d2a411dae9f99b2fb7a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282442} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d211f25-e2cd-5909-922b-140d4cb824ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283992}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e9aefc0f-4bcf-5840-a6a1-0c2bd30bd718" :question/math-academy-id "q-177649" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[-1,1]\\times [-i,i].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[-1,1]\\times [-0.5,0.5]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [-1,1],b\\in [-0.5,0.5]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(1,-0.5),$ $(1,0.5),$ $(-1,0.5),$ and $(-1,-0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/f0/f0a530434b8ac38fdb4cb517f22e121892c8b7c635c702c1cd9fccb2961aee18.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[-1,1]\\times [-i,i]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [-1,1],b\\in [-i,i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(1,-i),$ $(1,i),$ $(-1,i),$ and $(-1,-i).$\n\n![](images/69/6982658bd8ce0e3c81953309ed9f2a70d1e56bbfce8af8862a32da66bf19e638.png)\n\n \n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the line segment $[-1,1]\\times \\{0\\}:$\n\n![](images/34/34a3addbdcf3d5348805f494ed2e427f21f6ad424b0d9d2a411dae9f99b2fb7a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6290e701-b4ea-5a86-ab7e-7371c5bdc11e" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d30f87-aa1a-56e8-bb7e-4e9407b082ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b6/b6518f0f49f1147742d621fa940d49f84e7cce9c17d071fdfeb4a2e96abbf591.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282175} {:answer/id #uuid "bb664ede-5614-540b-b703-bceed826049a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/31/310ba014b846afb8d4f2bff610e762da71b47e8c4daa2d6ffebf4b62ecc4d1db.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283311} {:answer/id #uuid "bfe887dc-8e5c-5877-ae07-1a258f2dc9b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8c/8ce0c60aafe1a41b372c1f1477241c584d6f8ae224113c360576feb37fc25a8c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283358} {:answer/id #uuid "c2833ae2-8fd7-5c57-a212-e220f2f1e986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fc/fcda8aaa1da0ee1e9fee4957246497a927b4373c51d8a46db429540ea51f5083.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283383} {:answer/id #uuid "da0b515e-51b1-59bc-87bc-a56b64caa36d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cd/cd35c57fa9c6ce3ae2ee5961b8ae3e7d16ea1a2aa44c302a9e40f19b6c1b11ea.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfe887dc-8e5c-5877-ae07-1a258f2dc9b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8c/8ce0c60aafe1a41b372c1f1477241c584d6f8ae224113c360576feb37fc25a8c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283358} :answer-field/id #uuid "22b6eba5-0a47-5a04-bf53-140b1975630a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5dd76d07-a873-5a66-8b10-b721aee4da28" :question/math-academy-id "q-177652" :question/problem "Let $I=[-1,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [-|i|,|i|].$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=-0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{-0.5}=\\{-0.5\\}\\times [-0.5,0.5]=\\{(-0.5,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [-0.5,0.5]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(-0.5,-0.5)$ to the point $(-0.5,0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b7/b7793d85e02ccd05c55c34971c90be087d58274eabd21f46fe09f08ccd60797b.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [-|i|,|i|]=\\{(i,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [-|i|,|i|]\\}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,-|i|)$ to the point $(i,|i|).$ \n\n![](images/c3/c30712295adfe51c655662cc09f8f1e23b3ea97573693154e0e0b6ba48e15c07.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following figure that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/8c/8ce0c60aafe1a41b372c1f1477241c584d6f8ae224113c360576feb37fc25a8c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2aee319-68d6-54f7-8023-b24d32610bc4" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products of Special Sets in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eaa5394f-664d-516c-a7ca-0034c1aac434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/17/179fea73a29a658124583602bf26485b25ba70f66ca8187c47d745f46de25e1d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389890} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7583ed-df6d-5be7-bfdd-4f5596ff6fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/89/89ac9e71d8152097657f0c01daecf2b894dc142db4ba27fbfadcb8ded6e9cb19.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389891} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3bbeb0-b786-56a0-af4c-ce843e2f2a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b8/b8a268a69a978e7f9a14afd83c7c14735d797d4359826ae86f84873e53635363.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389892} {:answer/id #uuid "df54159c-0862-5afe-bf76-a3155b444d65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ac/acccce074e5dee93bbca149c16c5f7794dce17d1cd16432d25b0132382d877f8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389893} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c9bb19-93d6-5bb3-b166-5ed944544ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0a/0a03f883f977e67b9299d52e1572e484ed6010dc4f2555c7cbc2048f193dbc7f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb3bbeb0-b786-56a0-af4c-ce843e2f2a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b8/b8a268a69a978e7f9a14afd83c7c14735d797d4359826ae86f84873e53635363.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389892} :answer-field/id #uuid "21c822ca-1685-5918-acdb-d7b9f7059651" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2bbd8412-3c29-5dd3-ab23-10004aeed05b" :question/math-academy-id "q-181303" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=R\\times N$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=R\\times N\n$$\n\n \ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a real number and whose $y$-coordinate is a natural number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in R,\\,y\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S,$ consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/f8/f8808e4c35775c754dab0bf328a8d129e423009e18ec5f4b962461eba2afcea2.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $2.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}=\\{(x,2)\\,:\\,x\\in R\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/a5/a51fe9dc5bf7c55b01f72a45d4b88bde4653f0d3da85c1231b0d54c76a6e8c81.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets ${S}_{3},{S}_{4},{S}_{5},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product consists of the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\times N & ={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in N}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $R\\times N$ as the set of horizontal lines shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/7a/7ae3c488e60d3dcda304649e575a7d2efc54be7262a54d0455550af420c39b68.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2aee319-68d6-54f7-8023-b24d32610bc4" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products of Special Sets in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fa28e0c-1c51-5a6f-a7b1-03e689ebcc1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fa/fa1138d870b77845746ee708fac53399b76572b49bb8010d637e18787b54f0a9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284924} {:answer/id #uuid "6d53ede9-2317-5303-8661-bb0fe658f360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9d/9dd5b3d46da4f8ea1b6daf38356497243e48a23a833e8b6db2b06d8980f2d9c1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285794} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b62948-bf51-51f5-a4c5-8d9eabf1862d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/32/327fb02bbcd703a854e3d9d202bcb4b0b2995c9dd416045980b57385b21f937b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286479} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d02368-d0a1-5c58-9f25-e1ec8087391b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/14/141d0b84041957cf8415db4673c999f5213ff23553e57ab7e0e9120e648f306c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286744} {:answer/id #uuid "d87cf51a-8028-55c5-9b7d-3b01a0e1d775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/91/915321e31c69ec6f784a80d5195aae8c9467cb40911e12a2213cd3bd745a65c4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6d02368-d0a1-5c58-9f25-e1ec8087391b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/14/141d0b84041957cf8415db4673c999f5213ff23553e57ab7e0e9120e648f306c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286744} :answer-field/id #uuid "a33b316a-afb2-5626-82ed-6478dfaa2f2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d77329f-c53c-509c-8856-d83cfdd56ec9" :question/math-academy-id "q-181304" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=N\\times N$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=N\\times N\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a natural number and whose $y$-coordinate is a natural number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in N,\\,y\\in N\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in N\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/34/34f779801b1bb52d5834ab4e04c91d92585af9876f5ea687ad59cb6931e0144c.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}=\\{(2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in N\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/38/387709ae58ce7716338785f82e9159ce8570b046518554edd820c3ed31a23c53.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets ${S}_{3},{S}_{4},{S}_{5},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in N}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $N\\times N$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/14/141d0b84041957cf8415db4673c999f5213ff23553e57ab7e0e9120e648f306c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6290e701-b4ea-5a86-ab7e-7371c5bdc11e" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "458475cb-7c2d-5db3-9d9a-f7dcbf9640f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/07/070389fcdb6d69f9aa90dabbd98a0d3461e26d3e3e08b1d53b92e99688c09923.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285422} {:answer/id #uuid "56cc21dc-81f2-58b5-a405-76666971f42b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0f/0f219c170d7e73a8a5c3d11afabe6763e25ade77be9ed8a0b7495a8d9f6be90c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285585} {:answer/id #uuid "57df3629-2829-5e67-a0ee-b0af9d5c5261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/91/91f80f30887e5233d12ee814c1e991f81613bd52c9afd7334397b123b68b8bc7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285592} {:answer/id #uuid "71705615-b275-5206-9f46-e59b618b0dd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6b/6bc02e0957ea0099329b8266d4960b542d86c19f44b4fc811ba0752512def666.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285828} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ebacdf-8af4-5d1c-ad4f-a5eaba6a49e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/42/4233644fb8c5e19f379fdbc001951869fd5d9062e1f14d0abbb53d677780fb0a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "458475cb-7c2d-5db3-9d9a-f7dcbf9640f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/07/070389fcdb6d69f9aa90dabbd98a0d3461e26d3e3e08b1d53b92e99688c09923.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285422} :answer-field/id #uuid "88fca9fa-b9b5-5967-9c21-b7010d8c4956" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e98098c-88d7-594b-ad3c-687cf15456dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-181775" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=R\\times R$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=R\\times R\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in R,\\,y\\in R\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}=\\{(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/07/07a3d9a6c38b5bfcc529496735a1a66eaceefd5ae3437a2cb0cd45911eccafae.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in R$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}=\\{(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in R,$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line.\n\n![](images/e4/e454f1cf125486ca25acf15e26efd251a4a03b08e899814ab3e77db7898713c4.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $R:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in R}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nThis is the whole plane, as shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/07/070389fcdb6d69f9aa90dabbd98a0d3461e26d3e3e08b1d53b92e99688c09923.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198802 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3a2b291-c6dd-58c8-a10f-d851511d7bfc" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d13ed47-f553-5fa0-9b0c-fc3520c71290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c5/c5fdae9b803df3873ee7deef4a36678e0d8274dd256fe331360261f1fe6dd492.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285049} {:answer/id #uuid "4cb4e5e0-1e33-5a54-9313-e9da4923d084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c5/c51d37fab2b0a877c52c3b359156a5dbede97186f9565beeaab876a7e0c11714.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285504} {:answer/id #uuid "63fdf0b7-6f7a-514c-b3d5-f2ee4cad5afc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/eb/eb0433cbb5aa88f931fc36a215df435752acf7131096a1963527a1c4060eb64f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285698} {:answer/id #uuid "9939591f-e27f-5265-b89c-dc7f884d4938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d4a4810b3c298457d7944f69a993b6800755658b3b464491ebf780a478e5ca9b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286190} {:answer/id #uuid "b4d2471e-7365-57bd-8a3a-8b7f75527315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/65/65b35809a977ffa56218075e6b71645ccaa9db318eda972af051daed9d6ab3a6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d13ed47-f553-5fa0-9b0c-fc3520c71290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c5/c5fdae9b803df3873ee7deef4a36678e0d8274dd256fe331360261f1fe6dd492.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285049} :answer-field/id #uuid "b01d01b2-0cef-5747-a7ad-e3178a7a8069" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24f0a183-4542-54dd-8464-0891330af854" :question/math-academy-id "q-181949" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=\\{0,1,2\\}\\times \\{-1,1\\}$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, computing $\\{0,1,2\\}\\times \\{-1,1\\}$ gives the following set:\n\n$$\nS=\\{(0,-1),(0,1),(1,-1),(1,1),(2,-1),(2,1)\\}.\n$$\n\nOur visualization of this set is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/c5/c5fdae9b803df3873ee7deef4a36678e0d8274dd256fe331360261f1fe6dd492.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389909 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2aee319-68d6-54f7-8023-b24d32610bc4" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products of Special Sets in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c52fa43-923f-576a-ba23-dee22206f178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c9/c9adb78f087651508a43514756abbc45170766d6bb14a069053c4bf71e78e0a3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389911} {:answer/id #uuid "ae96fe3d-4eb2-5715-aab5-91382649a4ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d42f10aac16e2c7405fbf158dacb1b46137cc03800f8660d0ff4cfe11c9edc63.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389912} {:answer/id #uuid "2db12bff-09e6-5312-965d-054d7f6b4fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/16/16ff13c793d3c3f57eefee638fbc1ff83569ef6d084d9d053f8585f72c8812d7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389913} {:answer/id #uuid "6f56907b-5366-5f06-9fae-bd37aae2b8cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9b/9b6a2c5b3c9fdded8d615980df00228e2637515af0a23f62ae58b891bec3e3e7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389914} {:answer/id #uuid "5924e649-be02-5520-9d5e-94f6d2c07e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a1/a1b02e904c1df760f47d623d3ff17538c284d7ef6125b786165113a383c79c3c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2db12bff-09e6-5312-965d-054d7f6b4fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/16/16ff13c793d3c3f57eefee638fbc1ff83569ef6d084d9d053f8585f72c8812d7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389913} :answer-field/id #uuid "afa6976a-3c32-54c7-bedf-912fa5e61648" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9854e016-8489-5582-ad5c-ffa3a5b6e5ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-181959" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=N\\times Z$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=N\\times Z\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a natural number and whose $y$-coordinate is an integer number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in N,\\,y\\in Z\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any integer number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in Z\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/17/179fdaa3921cb29f2d25ff97bce262fd13fb2ff591c12e97a33953e95967f6fc.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}=\\{(2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in Z\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/73/7399e42988df8a809013393d8873b6a6e5f60b64c0419eadd7bb3c334eb410d6.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets ${S}_{3},{S}_{4},{S}_{5},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in N}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $N\\times Z$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/16/16ff13c793d3c3f57eefee638fbc1ff83569ef6d084d9d053f8585f72c8812d7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287777 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2aee319-68d6-54f7-8023-b24d32610bc4" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products of Special Sets in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27c5a7b9-c0be-5639-915c-03884b5490fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/80/80c13426f812f1e98b0ffd61d81eeb7c70a04c5013625d6e6d2add5f2d4a6d85.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285133} {:answer/id #uuid "2e31c3dd-ac87-5811-9f25-0539bdb01071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2d/2df87b90d770a5f2c0ba40a55330409d1cd80866b7e34299eab6dcbf675c6a13.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285199} {:answer/id #uuid "353d5395-bd32-522b-a142-64b30834c8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/de/de19fcf0f246b09d4bb957568e026b36de3f55c1a6c7065d79faacee794a8326.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285276} {:answer/id #uuid "976cc1f6-f8e9-5c10-b255-7a0a8509e457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/46/463ae2387423a48dd557af8cfd9b01b6bc08b95f1b3c2f337c6b0c53d3731fa2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286165} {:answer/id #uuid "ffe648c6-044b-5e2a-9bcf-8461bdafce50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8d/8de1a050eed07445dd4a80be2809e275419238f72e098693bfc1642a9e714403.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "353d5395-bd32-522b-a142-64b30834c8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/de/de19fcf0f246b09d4bb957568e026b36de3f55c1a6c7065d79faacee794a8326.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285276} :answer-field/id #uuid "b02b9fc4-15c4-59a7-9354-5da005f35049" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287513}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8fc924c0-3fd1-5974-a50f-be993c31ee9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-181966" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=Z\\times Z$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=Z\\times Z\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is an integer number and whose $y$-coordinate is an integer number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in Z,\\,y\\in Z\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any integer number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}=\\{(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in Z\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/96/9673951b4e72ba503e740369462f9e528e43ffc083706ee558ade7ccd52702f5.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any integer number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}=\\{(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in Z\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/79/797b66a293eb241f841869abe97e324f4301907f71029acceefd68487bef1b4f.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-3},{S}_{-2},{S}_{1},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =…\\cup {S}_{-3}\\cup {S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup \\text{ }{S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}… \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in Z}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $Z\\times Z$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/de/de19fcf0f246b09d4bb957568e026b36de3f55c1a6c7065d79faacee794a8326.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2aee319-68d6-54f7-8023-b24d32610bc4" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products of Special Sets in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "175fd771-7284-5f86-bac0-58e275c913f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/35/35b2f7b26a964f8892ba85bcdeb4fae5312d515044e355cc6a1f989efc8a825c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284997} {:answer/id #uuid "69b4a67b-e01f-5453-9e0c-c6c9eae81b79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3e/3ea69cc945f29707432415ed194c8abdec6b60056c8c64c845f27b3139cbd3d8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285756} {:answer/id #uuid "97fff838-44b9-5102-ad38-caeb329f009e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e3/e3550a78d58d91efb3eb012cfad691ee22b7bd216de7910850a289db3ab9e2b2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286177} {:answer/id #uuid "cc458a2c-8c16-5c32-b2c2-5ea40273286f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a7/a756e53554cb9184d96a52b83038fbd6b00b21d0a12cc658aebb5010e917fd03.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286649} {:answer/id #uuid "fc0afd0a-e1e2-5639-b18e-16cb8904338d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2d/2df87b90d770a5f2c0ba40a55330409d1cd80866b7e34299eab6dcbf675c6a13.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc458a2c-8c16-5c32-b2c2-5ea40273286f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a7/a756e53554cb9184d96a52b83038fbd6b00b21d0a12cc658aebb5010e917fd03.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286649} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b20ec3b-d5fd-5fc1-8858-23f125419c12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93d5eecd-9d38-5be6-abbe-17d9f9d1df54" :question/math-academy-id "q-181979" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={Z}^{-}\\times {Z}^{-}$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS={Z}^{-}\\times {Z}^{-}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a negative integer and whose $y$-coordinate is a negative integer.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,y\\in {Z}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is negative integer.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}=\\{(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {Z}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/37/37ad5627c3fb7cc89e751bb697e01ac7fecaf2712e230b6e3812ad9137d5cd46.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{-2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any negative integer.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-2}=\\{(-2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {Z}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/97/97ebcac85477b8e88564ab67d59c926d5faa72138c8a31d80d3b89895f33668c.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…{S}_{-5},{S}_{-4},{S}_{-3}$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =…{S}_{-5}\\cup {S}_{-4}\\cup {S}_{-3}\\cup {S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1} \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in {Z}^{-}}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize ${Z}^{-}\\times {Z}^{-}$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/a7/a756e53554cb9184d96a52b83038fbd6b00b21d0a12cc658aebb5010e917fd03.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6290e701-b4ea-5a86-ab7e-7371c5bdc11e" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72d6c485-e050-55c8-9679-fd6d97aa00e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/96/96a29779da824d7d2dc7b6d4f2b9c781a4a593b58e44f491724221c77888e3e3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389925} {:answer/id #uuid "08a4e04e-4888-5403-95d8-f078acf2c991" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e5/e5b130683075dd04e4b5129065d32b4d75b3dabfaff0b05b90de858b5e0f2961.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389926} {:answer/id #uuid "c1e8e5e1-7a36-52d6-b8df-aa671398b7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/97/97a74b119ddb8a618d6564bc077d03a5a4ceb7152702beb3682f2eab1a436b70.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389927} {:answer/id #uuid "66761d80-0b06-5258-89e9-adc40f67af90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/28/288ca0010ecc1fada05a67637b583a6e86b7f805d4e272e91563a13c18fc164a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389928} {:answer/id #uuid "09687f1b-acf3-52b9-85d2-f72a782bfbfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/3332464bdc0583c6ce99bf126805abaf57461e67aee6bdf12c95e11042baf9c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1e8e5e1-7a36-52d6-b8df-aa671398b7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/97/97a74b119ddb8a618d6564bc077d03a5a4ceb7152702beb3682f2eab1a436b70.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389927} :answer-field/id #uuid "46ec56ed-6fc0-52ed-aa83-998bc8081175" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c70aae50-ffb5-59f2-930c-cbbe5d9bb642" :question/math-academy-id "q-181985" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=[-1,0]\\times [-1,1]$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=[-1,0]\\times [-1,1]\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,0]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,0],\\,y\\in [-1,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}=\\{(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/c9/c93f3ad399b88ccbaac990f8f73e93cfdcb1192f52b9b12f2d3ce178776fa13b.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in [-1,0]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}=\\{(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]\\}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in [-1,0],$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line segment from the point $(i,-1)$ to the point $(i,1).$\n\n![](images/65/6557201d202a401a92ee37c9a69eab9ab6ab87c6342dbb9d2afebae30141346f.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $I=[-1,0]:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following rectangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/97/97a74b119ddb8a618d6564bc077d03a5a4ceb7152702beb3682f2eab1a436b70.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3a2b291-c6dd-58c8-a10f-d851511d7bfc" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb0b49a-e727-5e96-8f08-b6642b88f5fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/21/21119e9bd9b5a183cbf686891ba1b1fb33f645fbff27f1e088af5a88e5eea026.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560430} {:answer/id #uuid "3f98f313-1f05-5432-9f13-6963c25952a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a4/a4b3570ea09a38f044c6926f0516ddf9c42f9af6953422e3f2b90bca07bf70e9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560506} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef1cf93-ea8f-5c4a-bd63-007805fb0442" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f7/f7cecda03e84263537cb29bbd14bb4dccc2e60fada10db1ca96798490e978676.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560661} {:answer/id #uuid "c442a1fb-c5aa-593e-8502-90bebc8b66ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/13a0024b41d50d0ad22f790246e17ec19ce1e9bf91c7e2fe734bfcbdb9a00ef9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560754} {:answer/id #uuid "d7da440a-e81b-550c-ac55-bea9848fa4dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b8/b871bd5b8829c981f43bfbf8c051d50ee7a389df6c706f5d48fd07e167d9a66e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ef1cf93-ea8f-5c4a-bd63-007805fb0442" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f7/f7cecda03e84263537cb29bbd14bb4dccc2e60fada10db1ca96798490e978676.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560661} :answer-field/id #uuid "120de378-6c5c-5a20-a5a4-fe230e702451" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "871c3eee-78f1-5d74-b0c7-258b8f08a0ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-182004" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=\\{-2,1,2\\}\\times [0,2]$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=\\{-2,1,2\\}\\times [0,2]\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is either $-2,1,$ or $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2].$\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in \\{-2,1,2\\},\\,y\\in [0,2]\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(-2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [0,2]\\}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/44/449b948df4a32c540281ddac1659c261e2908433ecc1f383b26cb5cb4aa29756.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}=\\{(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [0,2]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/92/922c96e62e8ed3481e595595e060956fbaf191cd3ec7636e7a874b11fea3bcd5.png)\n\nNow, consider ${S}_{3}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}=\\{(2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [0,2]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/0d/0d3cb62f7e9fb47823d0a2ba8c071e09adbea673ad54a5d1b014e8882aeff472.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the three line segments shown below.\n\n![](images/f7/f7cecda03e84263537cb29bbd14bb4dccc2e60fada10db1ca96798490e978676.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287870 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3a2b291-c6dd-58c8-a10f-d851511d7bfc" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bc30aef-a200-5e7b-b630-f12a3f8e50de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/54/54fd8fa56f44e0a4c0e3c162d6262afab99c61b565ae2bc5b2e7bcf2f9295137.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284884} {:answer/id #uuid "3437e92b-7dd8-58db-82c3-7fe58132b3ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c4/c454c6108cb57c16ff806fb92cd95cb4b97e8077e1038bfb3164ac1d3666f761.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285269} {:answer/id #uuid "40b1b676-8681-56a5-bbc4-ce7e67038eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e7/e75d513154aa16dc2ef43b24a03f8375a96ed52edd1c43d8a59798674c17585b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285391} {:answer/id #uuid "db7398b2-0747-50e6-8e61-8607506d3441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/12/12b910d75a864171898a8ee8874245a684e8c943efb27c9b755c5d31ef322af7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286785} {:answer/id #uuid "f4bad6bb-2de3-5fb3-a582-055326420b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5d/5dd3ff71d17188adaa68632b6d16aed1f41e1975ec4ddd321a8160fabb0e16b8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4bad6bb-2de3-5fb3-a582-055326420b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5d/5dd3ff71d17188adaa68632b6d16aed1f41e1975ec4ddd321a8160fabb0e16b8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287031} :answer-field/id #uuid "90e1e4a8-170d-53c4-8e08-20f6a5548efa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08598431-bbb6-5074-989f-295156a85943" :question/math-academy-id "q-184488" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=\\{-2,2\\}\\times \\{-1,0,1\\}$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, computing $\\{-2,2\\}\\times \\{-1,0,1\\}$ gives the following set:\n\n$$\nS=\\{(-2,-1),(-2,0),(-2,1),(2,-1),(2,0),(2,1)\\}.\n$$\n\nOur visualization of this set is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/5d/5dd3ff71d17188adaa68632b6d16aed1f41e1975ec4ddd321a8160fabb0e16b8.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390326 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3a2b291-c6dd-58c8-a10f-d851511d7bfc" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "607f5fc0-710c-50ec-853a-f1cbe588f0cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/09b74d8a7baf8c22cab4ad3841e53c7286cd72dd7523916544ea370595b199a9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390328} {:answer/id #uuid "f8387a2d-e7fd-51de-b176-ea56d9e540b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2e/2eec72a5444533c1bb4f86836cf8479b76ae38d69c35f5f5eef5fd313a2365f0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390329} {:answer/id #uuid "36db9686-690f-54ec-bfac-28a409caed44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/01/01d87db018bcbbf013d7f33519418849fe70e0d772870335482a7b07cfc89fd9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390330} {:answer/id #uuid "c165510a-291f-5076-b75f-5f046b3f04a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/70/70f7c02b3bca2b816858eaef766b5bbf3ced8d8abf101ef38ecda19b73781ee3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390331} {:answer/id #uuid "9f87f4ca-c61a-584a-8253-8ab30a3d9929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/aa/aa3411e662566a609de5163269dbc1e7c0ad92f415b52936c5ef568d7058d2d2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390332}] :a