this set is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/86/86598866633d3a49c13cf979b0c2c9de74d147e4584a1c6a88847434bc9d3bbf.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287873 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6290e701-b4ea-5a86-ab7e-7371c5bdc11e" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "124b6724-8247-5a30-a27e-64ee27a7b9ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f6/f6d06dbdcf69c4dba1d0375bbe204151c7a5d8098f7385220f3c66f35f7fa0a8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284951} {:answer/id #uuid "5457000a-5402-53be-84a9-6c25cd0447bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/11/119379ee56b15559073a7fefc9100dc8145f376c28271155fc10d9bac7a7594f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285563} {:answer/id #uuid "87bb1e80-85e0-5bf4-ab3a-251ecf0f3d12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/71/714c5db9aceb568a4988ce38a32e73a186178939fe0ba48cd384b3cf88f0e937.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286031} {:answer/id #uuid "d70164e9-ba10-59a6-bf82-d75501cda8d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5b/5b5715ba2a1b71a9f5aef52882ed62ba2fe1610c143224914430f79fdc8f06b5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286747} {:answer/id #uuid "fc17a4a5-9d67-5ff7-af17-7d8286424034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c9/c9ba946ca63983aece16f5243680fe8cc7dddf930f4d284fd50b7b2fbb6255dc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d70164e9-ba10-59a6-bf82-d75501cda8d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5b/5b5715ba2a1b71a9f5aef52882ed62ba2fe1610c143224914430f79fdc8f06b5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286747} :answer-field/id #uuid "701d2b5a-8084-518d-9ff1-07d16784e20e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f55227ad-192f-5284-8e39-2f59b086abb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-184504" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times \\{1-i\\}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[-0.5,0.5]\\times \\{0.5\\}=\\{(k,0.5)\\,:\\,k\\in [-0.5,0.5]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(-0.5,0.5)$ to the point $(0.5,0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/509d3e8d3bce0b422cad7e7f02377468cacc0de3a4e45647c12fef15f2c9991f.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times \\{1-i\\}=\\{(k,1-i)\\,:\\,k\\in [-i,i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(-i,1-i)$ to the point $(i,1-i).$ \n\n![](images/21/21859c2ac02ba80d47672bf2fab25f7358feb921bc5b546c1e8c783c2819bea3.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/5b/5b5715ba2a1b71a9f5aef52882ed62ba2fe1610c143224914430f79fdc8f06b5.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287874 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6290e701-b4ea-5a86-ab7e-7371c5bdc11e" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "113ca175-2712-5014-9077-85078286751b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e4/e460699a3844c0e295af363760cdb8d4ce9ad54bc00c051ca517e4b7614db982.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284938} {:answer/id #uuid "428273f8-7974-5984-8271-b2e8847df542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e1/e1d3407dfca8c57d9b7c14431260d91ec1fd60e312ecd2846026e0667a421cf2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285402} {:answer/id #uuid "5f436de7-6002-51df-b081-59d859db9a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ee/ee6257f32003e385616c0e1f57f76ae9e9c23fd09f7348202a8f26433ac24056.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285659} {:answer/id #uuid "7a79a816-2098-5166-83da-f6d6033a3276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4d/4d860b60ab9e139b26c9f6e1d330188d5e752a51624a2374ad713b6974e66608.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285919} {:answer/id #uuid "9d80cf71-4dc6-5b58-b1e4-1d51f7478b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0f/0ff3c422678e1cb1c68a60f4957620e338095aa349f274338909886c2e6ed1e0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a79a816-2098-5166-83da-f6d6033a3276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4d/4d860b60ab9e139b26c9f6e1d330188d5e752a51624a2374ad713b6974e66608.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285919} :answer-field/id #uuid "28a97ff9-a063-55b4-b93b-60e422e8289a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c878a8c-80cf-5939-80cc-1ff04a9bef2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-184506" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,2]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [-i,i].$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}=\\{1\\}\\times [-1,1]=\\{(1,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [-1,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(1,-1)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/f2/f26fa8a525806370f5505ad097ead2b289192bb3a6eb3e341eb7c2f91a03531f.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [-i,i]=\\{(i,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [-i,i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,-i)$ to the point $(i,i).$ \n\n![](images/bf/bfeafe4c3b800b33b4f8550de02c2eb908effb5c28ef59b40f8c5e2bcad38ac4.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/4d/4d860b60ab9e139b26c9f6e1d330188d5e752a51624a2374ad713b6974e66608.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287877 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5793f07d-e0de-5707-a5e1-32d657244e0b" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Intersections of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35b6f556-6366-5615-9f38-778d78dcf377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/58/581e4aec0613b738b5978db3f527ad481228a4610e0576930311115c190e0535.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285282} {:answer/id #uuid "9e5e8d45-32b8-5cc2-9732-84dbe5a5ebce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/19/19a2cd951a55508269a0034aec582345bf7e350ec516fe1eecac0d6bf5847981.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286237} {:answer/id #uuid "a06aa94c-f938-5fe8-90b5-b2eb33859e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/08/08ca3b1dd409fa953338c05f2089772ec78a0b64da1b131f82d6d9f02afd7c1e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286250} {:answer/id #uuid "c260ef53-ea55-5197-863e-22d0b862f58d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4cc675d39196f4dc1ddb2b4c6cdff04acf077d455a476aba36a13152c4d9e83c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286567} {:answer/id #uuid "d4c459aa-d2e5-5f21-9a69-47a4556816a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5d/5d83de0d0c317ac7663e607f826251a541017464a8e0ffa7b4c322a0443f7781.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e5e8d45-32b8-5cc2-9732-84dbe5a5ebce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/19/19a2cd951a55508269a0034aec582345bf7e350ec516fe1eecac0d6bf5847981.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286237} :answer-field/id #uuid "02b5162c-41d5-56e0-ba71-34aaf7b04651" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e59a2427-468e-5dd7-9dc4-516ebb0d95d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-184530" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,1]\\times [0,i].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0,1]\\times [0,0.5]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,1],b\\in [0,0.5]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(0.5,1),$ and $(0.5,0)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/0f/0fef44c4b8c4911a892d7dad4502edbb80ef236553d6fddb57de1472bd44a62b.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,1]\\times [0,i]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,1],b\\in [0,i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(i,1),$ and $(i,0).$\n\n![](images/f4/f4602a46d3e4fc1799a475f05548ef278fdd33d354d1ec19ca4e5c5cc34cfcf8.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the line segments $[0,1]\\times \\{0\\}:$\n\n![](images/19/19a2cd951a55508269a0034aec582345bf7e350ec516fe1eecac0d6bf5847981.png)"}]}
